"rev": 1,
"upd": "2026-10-29",
"html": "\n<div class=\"iointro\">Dx PAD ใช้ <span class=\"imp\">ABI</span> (★ ผู้สอน; &lt;0.90 = PAD) · ถ้า calcified (DM, ESRD) ABI &gt;1.40 → ใช้ <span class=\"imp\">TBI</span> · anatomic imaging (duplex/CTA/MRA/angiogram) ทำเมื่อจะ revascularize เท่านั้น · CLI 1 ปี: ตาย 25%, ตัดขา 30%</div>\n<div class=\"box\"><h3>Ankle–Brachial Index (วิธีวัด)<span class=\"ref\">p13</span></h3>\n<div class=\"fig\">{{IMG:l9912_abi_pic}}</div>\n<ul><li><span class=\"hw\">doppler ฟัง brachial a. (เอาข้างที่ได้ SBP สูงกว่ามาคิด)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"hw\">doppler ฟัง posterior tibial / dorsalis pedis — เอา SBP ของ vessel ที่มีค่าสูงกว่ามาคิด</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"box\"><h3>สูตร + แปลผล ABI ★<span class=\"ref\">p14</span> <span class=\"chip x\">★ ผู้สอน</span></h3>\n<div class=\"fig\">{{IMG:l9912_abi_calc}}</div>\n<table class=\"fx\"><tr><th>ABI</th><th>แปลผล</th></tr>\n<tr><td><span class=\"imp\">&gt; 0.90</span></td><td>Normal <span class=\"hw\">(&lt;0.90 = PAD)</span></td></tr><tr><td>0.71–0.90</td><td>Mild obstruction</td></tr><tr><td>0.41–0.70</td><td>Moderate obstruction</td></tr><tr><td>0.00–0.40</td><td>Severe obstruction</td></tr></table>\n<div>Right ABI = highest right ankle pressure ÷ highest arm pressure · Left เช่นเดียวกัน · ตัวอย่าง 92/164 = <span class=\"imp\">0.56</span> = moderate obstruction (highest ankle / highest brachial ถูก highlight)</div>\n<div class=\"mn\"><b class=\"k\">\"9-7-4-0\"</b> = &gt;0.9 ปกติ · 0.7–0.9 mild · 0.4–0.7 moderate · &lt;0.4 severe</div></div>\n<div class=\"box\"><h3>Diagnostic testing for suspected PAD (ACC/AHA 2024)<span class=\"ref\">p15</span></h3>\n<div class=\"fig\">{{IMG:l9912_dx_flow}}</div>\n<ul><li>History + PE สงสัย PAD → <span class=\"imp\">ABI ± segmental limb pressures &amp; waveforms (Class I)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"imp\">Noncompressible arteries, ABI &gt; 1.40</span> <span class=\"hw\">e.g. DM, ESRD → calcified vessel = cuff กดไม่ได้ └ เอา ABI มาใช้ไม่ได้</span> → <span class=\"imp\">TBI (Class I)</span> <span class=\"hw\">= วัด toe pressure แทน (ใช้ laser วัดที่ digital a.) └ calcified น้อยกว่า</span>\n<br/>TBI Normal (&gt;0.70) → search alternative dx (Table 5) · Abnormal (≤0.70) <span class=\"hw\">วงกลม: = PAD</span></li>\n<li>ABI Normal 1.00–1.40 / Borderline 0.91–0.99 → ถ้ามี exertional non-joint leg symptoms → <span class=\"imp\">Exercise ABI (Class I)</span> ; ไม่มี → alternative dx</li>\n<li>Abnormal ABI ≤0.90 → Exercise ABI (Class IIa)</li>\n<li>Lifestyle-limiting claudication ทั้งที่ได้ GDMT และพิจารณา revascularization → <span class=\"imp\">Anatomic assessment</span>: duplex US / CTA / MRA (Class I) หรือ invasive angiography (Class IIa) · ไม่ → continue GDMT (Class I)</li>\n<li><span class=\"imp\">Do not perform invasive or noninvasive anatomic assessments for asymptomatic patients (Class III: Harm)</span> · สงสัย CLI → ดู Figure 2</li></ul>\n<div class=\"warn\"><span class=\"chip e\">เสริม</span> Guideline ล่าสุด 2024 ACC/AHA ใช้คำว่า CLTI และแนะนำ resting ABI เป็น first-line; ใน suspected CLTI เพิ่ม toe pressure/TBI, TcPO2 หรือ skin perfusion pressure ได้ {{R:1}}</div></div>\n<div class=\"box\"><h3>Natural history ของ claudication (Hirsch 2006 ACC/AHA)<span class=\"ref\">p16</span></h3>\n<div class=\"fig\">{{IMG:l9912_natural}}</div>\n<table class=\"fx\"><tr><th>กลุ่ม (PAD ≥50 ปี)</th><th>สัดส่วน</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Asymptomatic</td><td>20–50%</td></tr><tr><td>Other leg pain</td><td>30–40%</td></tr><tr><td>Typical claudication</td><td>10–35%</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"imp\">Critical limb ischemia</span></td><td>1–3%</td></tr></table>\n<ul><li><span class=\"imp\">CLI 1-year outcomes</span>: alive with two limbs <span class=\"imp\">45%</span> · <span class=\"imp\">amputation 30%</span> · <span class=\"imp\">mortality 25%</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"imp\">5-year outcomes (claudicant)</span>: limb morbidity — stable claudication 70–80% · worsening 10–20% · CLI 5–10% <span class=\"hw\">↓↓ → amputation</span> ; CV morbidity &amp; mortality <span class=\"hw\">MI</span> — non-fatal CV event (MI/stroke) 20% · mortality 10–15% (CV causes 75%, non-CV 25%)</li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"box\"><h3>CTA and Angiogram<span class=\"ref\">p17</span></h3>\n<div class=\"fig\">{{IMG:l9912_ctangio}}</div>\n<div><span class=\"hw\">= mapping before revascularization → localize lesion</span> · ภาพขวา (angiogram) ลายมือ: <span class=\"hw\">Aortoiliac</span></div></div>\n",
